--TEST--
`->$name` and `->{expr}` are `E0235` in every position a member is named — read, write, call and `?->` — never a panic below the checker, per ADR 0014 § 5
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Box {
    public string $name = "a";
    public function label(): string { return "l"; }
}
var $b = new Box();
string $n = "name";
// ADR 0014 § 5's compile-time half, taken over the *spelling*: `->$name`
// names a member only when the statement runs, and there is nothing for
// the checker to resolve it against.
echo $b->$n, "\n";
// `->{expr}` is the same construct written the other way, and a write
// target takes it exactly as a read does.
$b->{$n} = "z";
// A computed *method* name is the third spelling and the same refusal —
// the name in front of the parentheses is decided the same way.
echo $b->{"lab" . "el"}(), "\n";
// `?->` changes only whether the receiver is tested, never how the
// member is named.
echo $b?->$n, "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:11:10
   |
11 | echo $b->$n, "\n";
   |          ^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: ADR 0014 § 5 makes every property a declared name, so there is nothing for a computed one to resolve against — write the member out, or hold data whose keys are only known at run time in an `array<string, T>`

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:14:5
   |
14 | $b->{$n} = "z";
   |     ^^^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: ADR 0014 § 5 makes every property a declared name, so there is nothing for a computed one to resolve against — write the member out, or hold data whose keys are only known at run time in an `array<string, T>`

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:17:10
   |
17 | echo $b->{"lab" . "el"}(), "\n";
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: ADR 0014 § 5 makes every property a declared name, so there is nothing for a computed one to resolve against — write the member out, or hold data whose keys are only known at run time in an `array<string, T>`

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:20:11
   |
20 | echo $b?->$n, "\n";
   |           ^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: ADR 0014 § 5 makes every property a declared name, so there is nothing for a computed one to resolve against — write the member out, or hold data whose keys are only known at run time in an `array<string, T>`

